From b1377abb4063fb1435dbaeb833d11b246ee373cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:48:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ARM64: config.guess: recognize aarch64 Cygwin build
 machines

A native configure on the aarch64-pc-cygwin runtime with a CYGWIN_NT
uname fell through to "unable to guess system type"; only the i*
and x86_64 Cygwin cases existed.  Cross builds pass --host and are
unaffected.

Signed-off-by: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
---
 build-aux/config.guess | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build-aux/config.guess b/build-aux/config.guess
index e81d3ae..6e29f97 100644
--- a/build-aux/config.guess
+++ b/build-aux/config.guess
@@ -947,6 +947,9 @@ EOF
     amd64:CYGWIN*:*:* | x86_64:CYGWIN*:*:*)
 	GUESS=x86_64-pc-cygwin
 	;;
+    aarch64:CYGWIN*:*:*)
+	GUESS=aarch64-pc-cygwin
+	;;
     prep*:SunOS:5.*:*)
 	SUN_REL=`echo "$UNAME_RELEASE" | sed -e 's/[^.]*//'`
 	GUESS=powerpcle-unknown-solaris2$SUN_REL
-- 
2.56.1

